  * flex_prefill.py
        <- minference/modules/flexprefill.py

Local modifications (the file header carries a short pointer to this list):
  1. the flash_attn-missing fallback's relative import
     (`from ..ops.flash_attn_triton import ...`) is rewritten to a clear
     ImportError so the module loads standalone (flash_attn is a hard dep here;
     the error message names the install command);
  2. the upstream `__main__` smoke block is removed;
  3. in `get_active_blocks` the vertical/slash block-budget divisor was changed
     from a hardcoded `// 128` to `// block_size`, so a non-128 block_size (a
     valid {16,32,64,128} knob) yields the correct block count instead of a
     budget scaled by block_size/128;
  4. a hardcoded `x = x.to("cuda")` in `triton_bnhd_pool` was removed — it moved
     the input to the default device and corrupted results under accelerate
     device_map layer sharding (x already arrives on its layer's device);
  5. the prefill-kernel block_size assert MESSAGE was corrected from
     "{16,32,64,128}" to "{32,64,128}" to match the set it actually checks (the
     prefill kernel does not support block_size 16; only the decode sibling
     does) — message-only, the checked set is unchanged.
  6. a block of commented-out "torch implementation" dead code in
     `triton_column_count_cumsum` (superseded by the Triton `count_kernel`) was
     removed — comment-only, no executable change.

No algorithmic change was made: the Triton kernels and the gamma/tau
block-selection logic keep their exact upstream behavior; the file was
reformatted to this repo's style (black/isort, line length 99) with logic
unchanged. Numerics match flash dense at high gamma (rel ~0.0015 @ gamma=0.99 on
a Qwen3-8B shape, verified in this environment).

